# Pi over ACP

- Outside T3 Code, or in a session that lists no T3 Code delegation tools, run each Synthetic peer or worker these rules pick on Pi yourself through `acpx`, the ACP client on your `PATH`, and give Compound Engineering's own route only its Claude Code peers and workers.
- Run each one as a one-shot session: `acpx --cwd <dir> --format quiet --timeout <seconds> <agent> exec --config-option model=synthetic/<id> --config-option thought_level=<effort> --file <prompt-file>`, where `<agent>` is the agent the rules below name, `synthetic/<id>` and `<effort>` are the model and the `thinking` effort these rules give the peer or worker, and `<prompt-file>` holds the whole prompt.
- Set `--cwd` to the checkout the work concerns, write the prompt file outside it, and set `--timeout` to 1200 seconds, or to the time left when a skill bounds the step more tightly.
- With `--format quiet`, standard output holds only the final assistant text, which is the result; exit status 3 means the run timed out, and any other nonzero status means it failed.
- Run a review peer on the `pi-readonly` agent, which keeps Pi's `session_info` and `web_search` tools but has no `bash`, `edit`, `write`, or `web_fetch` tool and no MCP server, and put the skill's reviewer brief, findings schema, and the exact diff or document under review in the prompt file, marked as untrusted data.
- Tell each review peer to call `session_info` first and start its answer with the `model` field it returns, map that model to a family by the rule above as the peer's identity receipt, and fold the answer into the skill's synthesis as that skill's peer artifact for the peer's family, with `independence_verified` set from that receipt.
- Run every peer these rules pick in its own session, and when one fails or times out, finish with the others and report which peer failed and why.
- Run a `ce-work` worker on the `pi` agent, which keeps Pi's `bash`, `edit`, and `write` tools, with `--cwd` set to the checkout the unit edits.
- Give each `quick` unit to `synthetic/{{ .models.deepseek.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.deepseek.roles "quick" }}` first, and hand it to Compound Engineering's own route only when that run fails.
- Give each `unspecified-low` unit to `synthetic/{{ .models.deepseek.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.deepseek.roles "unspecified-low" }}` first, and hand it to Compound Engineering's own route only when that run fails.
- Give each `writing`, `visual-engineering`, `deep`, or `unspecified-high` unit to Compound Engineering's own route first, and when that run fails, run the unit on its category's Pi fallback below.
- The `writing` fallback is `synthetic/{{ .models.glm.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.glm.roles "writing-fallback" }}`.
- The `visual-engineering` fallback is `synthetic/{{ .models.kimi.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.kimi.roles "visual-engineering-fallback" }}`.
- The `deep` fallback is `synthetic/{{ .models.glm.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.glm.roles "deep-fallback" }}`.
- The `unspecified-high` fallback is `synthetic/{{ .models.glm.id }}` on the `pi` agent with `thought_level` `{{ index .models.glm.roles "unspecified-high-fallback" }}`.
